ys among them who sometimes talk idle talk and will not stop themselves from talking even in the Bhak, it is better that they keep their regularity in the room, and wrote in the letter of the Ramez (he is Rabbi Rabbi Moshe Makruta) that the correction should not be made at the beginning of the night, even in the summer, and not on the head of a reserve Second, but midnight and beyond, and sleep should be brought before the beginning of the night so that he can get up half an hour before daylight and at the hour of stress, even though it has risen, there is some reality for correcting the 20th day of the year, and there in B.C. 15 he wrote that in places where there are a lot of silihats in the Arah and in the Akhmort and also do the fall of noses, the one who usually makes midnight all year round has to make a correction in the Arah of the year as well. Refer there to the 16th sign. He who is used to saying tikkun at midnight and gets up in the amshurat and already in the sabbath say silihot and there is no leisure to say both of them, he will say tikkun at midnight according to the order of the late Ari Zal, which is a greater principle than the silihot and wrote in Barchi Yosef in the name of Mza Mahara Azulai (he has kindness to Abraham) For:
